Ownership: Graph

Purpose:
  Defines ownership model for graph nodes.

OwnerRoles:
  BUSINESS:
    Requirements, business rules
  BACKEND:
    Backend code, APIs
  FRONTEND:
    Frontend code, UI
  MOBILE:
    Mobile code
  QA:
    Tests, BDD
  SECURITY:
    Security controls, findings
  DEVOPS:
    Infrastructure, CI/CD
  DBA:
    Database, migrations
  SUPPORT:
    Runbooks, incidents

OwnershipRules:
  [OW1]  Every node SHOULD have an owner.
  [OW2]  Owner is responsible for accuracy.
  [OW3]  Ownership enables routing: "Who should handle this?"
  [OW4]  Secondary owners MAY be assigned.

IncidentRouting:
  Incident: INC-<ID>
    ↓
  Task: TASK-<ID>
    ↓
  Domain: <DOMAIN>
    ↓
  Primary: <LAYER>
  Secondary: <LAYER>
  Infrastructure: <LAYER>

DocumentationRouting:
  Source: ./<layer>/<domain>/<module>/<artifact>
    ↓
  Domain: <Domain>
    ↓
  Docs:
    - docs/<layer>/<domain>.md (<AUDIENCE>)
    - docs/<layer>/<domain>.md (<AUDIENCE>)
    - docs/<layer>/<domain>.md (<AUDIENCE>)
    - docs/<layer>/<domain>.md (<AUDIENCE>)

State: +
  